course: dictionary
lesson: 8531
title: Money words: savings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word savings has two main meanings, and the context tells you which one. «Ella put her birthday money into her savings.» Here savings means money she keeps and does not spend.
explain: The second meaning is about money or time you do not have to spend. «The shop gave a saving of 5 dollars on the coat.» Here a saving is money you keep because the coat was cheaper. Ask yourself: is someone keeping money, or not spending it?
explain: Savings is a plural noun, so it often ends in s, as in savings account. One single amount is a saving. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Savings means money that you keep and do not spend.
fact: «Savings» can also mean an amount of money or time you do not have to spend, like «a saving of 5 dollars».
fact: A savings account is kept at a bank, and the bank may pay you a little extra called interest.
fact: «A children's savings account grows with regular saving: £20 a month is £240 a year.»
fact: To make a saving means to avoid spending money, for example by buying something when it is on sale.
exercise: «Ella put her birthday money into her savings.» What are Ella's savings? | *Money she keeps and does not spend | Her favourite lunch | Presents she gave away | Toys she has broken
exercise: «The shop gave a saving of 5 dollars on the coat.» What does saving mean here? | Money you spend on a coat | A shop that is closed | *Money you do not have to spend | Five new coats
exercise: «£20 a month is £240 a year.» If you put £20 into savings every month, how much have you saved after one year? | £180 | *£240 | £2,400 | £120
test: Jayden asks what a savings account is. | A wooden money box | A list of all the jobs in the bank | *A bank account where you keep money and may earn a little interest | A shop card for buying sweets
test: «Ella's library fine came out of her savings.» Where did the money for the fine come from? | The library gave her the money | A loan from the bank | *The money she had kept and not spent | Her parents' wallet
exam: Which sentence uses savings to mean money kept and not spent? | *«Sam paid his pocket money into his savings.» | «Lara saved the goal in the final minute.» | «Dad made a saving by buying the cheaper bread.» | «The sale gave us a saving on shoes.»
